            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0468" n="396" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 560/48.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador
                    O’Brien.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-12-29"><hi rendition="#italic">December 29,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 872, of the 22d ultimo, inclosing a copy of the correspondence had between
                    the embassy and the consulate at Dalny on the subject of extraterritoriality in
                    the leased territory of Kwangtung Province.</p>
                <p>The department has informed the consulate at Dalny that it approves your
                    instruction on the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
